<Guide slug="africa-rainy-seasons" photo="maasai-mara">
  <p>
    Africa's safari regions have opposite rainy seasons. <strong>East Africa</strong> — Kenya, Tanzania, Uganda and Rwanda —
    has two: the <strong>long rains from March to May</strong> and the <strong>short rains in November</strong>, with dry
    seasons in between. <strong>Southern Africa</strong> — South Africa's Kruger, Botswana, Zimbabwe, Zambia and Namibia — has
    one summer rainy season from <strong>November to March</strong> and a long dry winter from May to October. Cape Town is the
    exception: it has a Mediterranean climate with winter rain from May to August.
  </p>

